{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQWNBysj71Zd6DYEyL7TiK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: ICLR 2027 (expected deadline ~October 2026; 5 months for full pipeline experiments)\n5\t- Backup: AAAI 2027 (abstract July 21, paper July 28, 2026 — tight, 2 months)\n6\t- Backup 2: EACL 2027 via ARR August 2026 cycle (August 3, 2026)\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条, 可证伪)\n9\t\n10\t**Claim 1 (Detection)**: DIF analysis across model release cohorts detects benchmark contamination with practical power (ETS C: TPR 0.72-0.85, FPR <0.05 at N≥80, δ≥1.4) and is robust to RL training — because it operates on group-level behavioral response patterns (correct/incorrect conditional on ability), not within-model output distributions that GRPO/PPO smoothing affects.\n11\t\n12\t**Claim 2 (Ensemble Coverage)**: A multi-signal contamination sentinel combining DIF (large effects, RL-robust), ConStat-style perturbation testing (non-RL models), and DVD generation variance (variant contamination) achieves detection coverage across the full effect-size spectrum and model-type landscape, with each signal covering the blind spots of the others.\n13\t\n14\t**Claim 3 (Regeneration)**: Bifactor IRT equating with anchor items enables psychometrically equivalent benchmark regeneration — flagged items can be replaced with empirically calibrated alternatives that preserve construct validity, difficulty, and discrimination, maintaining benchmark comparability through a formal graceful-degradation framework.\n15\t\n16\t## Story Spine\n17\t\n18\t**Problem**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent ability. Contamination systematically erodes this validity. Critically, RL training (GRPO/PPO) conceals contamination signals: Wang et al. (ICLR 2026) show 14-20pp AUROC degradation for all reference-free detectors after ~156 GRPO steps, reducing most to near-random (~50% AUROC). The model ecosystem is shifting toward RL-trained reasoning models (o1, o3, DeepSeek-R1), making this a growing threat.\n19\t\n20\t**Existing approaches & gaps**: LiveBench updates monthly from recent sources but applies no psychometric calibration across updates. ConStat provides FDR-controlled performance-based detection but relies on perturbation sensitivity that RL can mask. DVD detects variant contamination via generation variance but is untested against RL. Growing Pains (arXiv 2026) uses multidimensional IRT for extensible evaluation but addresses score comparability, not contamination. No existing work closes the full loop from RL-robust detection through construct-constrained generation to psychometrically equated regeneration.\n21\t\n22\t**Our framing**: Contamination is fundamentally a psychometric problem — it creates Differential Item Functioning (DIF), where contaminated items become differentially easier for exposed model cohorts beyond what general ability gains predict. DIF operates on group-level Item Characteristic Curves conditional on ability, making it orthogonal to within-model output distribution smoothing. This is the one contamination signal RL cannot conceal without negating the purpose of contamination itself: if a model memorized an item, it must answer it correctly, creating a detectable behavioral anomaly at the population level. Combined with a multi-signal ensemble for full effect-size coverage and bifactor IRT equating for calibrated item regeneration, this creates the first self-healing benchmark framework.\n23\t\n24\t**Headline result template**: \"On MMLU with 5,000+ models spanning 3 years of releases, DIF-based ETS C detection achieves 73-85% TPR with <5% FPR for large contamination effects (δ≥1.4), maintaining power where 10 existing detection methods degrade to near-random under RL training (Wang et al., ICLR 2026).\"\n25\t\n26\t## Venue Fit Risks\n27\t\n28\t- **ICLR**: Strong fit — evaluation methodology, robustness to RL, psychometric theory applied to ML. Risk: reviewers may not be familiar with IRT/DIF methodology. Mitigation: provide self-contained DIF tutorial in appendix, reproducible code, and connection to ML-familiar concepts (DIF ≈ \"fairness testing for items\").\n29\t- **Cross-discipline bridge**: IRT/psychometrics vocabulary needs translation for ML audience. Key mappings: \"examinees\" → \"models\", \"test items\" → \"benchmark questions\", \"DIF\" → \"item-level contamination signal\", \"equating\" → \"score comparability across benchmark versions\".\n30\t- **Novelty concern**: DIF itself is not new (1988). Our contribution is the novel application to LLM benchmark contamination + the RL-robustness argument + the integration with regeneration. Need to frame as \"bringing mature psychometric tools to solve an urgent ML problem\" rather than \"inventing new statistics.\"\n31\t\n32\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n33\t\n34\t1. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects (δ≥1.4)\"**\n35\t   - Response: Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most (GSM1K: 10-13% average accuracy drop). Small effects (δ<0.6) have minimal impact on rankings. For medium effects, the ensemble's other signals provide coverage.\n36\t   - Evidence needed: plan_001 (real-data validation), plan_003 (ensemble)\n37\t\n38\t2. **\"Model cohort sample sizes are too small for classical DIF\"**\n39\t   - Response: (a) ETS C uses effect-size thresholds, not p-values, reducing sample-size dependence; (b) annual cohorts now reach N=80-100; (c) Cumulative Bayesian priors accumulate power over time; (d) Item-Focused Trees treat release date as continuous covariate.\n40\t   - Evidence needed: plan_001 (real cohort sizes), plan_008 (Bayesian DIF, P2)\n41\t\n42\t3. **\"Only validated in simulation\"**\n43\t   - Response: plan_001 uses METABENCH real data (5,055 models). plan_004 cross-validates on GSM8K with GSM1K ground truth.\n44\t   - Evidence needed: plan_001, plan_004\n45\t\n46\t4. **\"Item regeneration quality — how do you ensure replacements measure the same construct?\"**\n47\t   - Response: Bifactor IRT equating with anchor items + empirical calibration via student simulation (not prompt-based difficulty targeting). Construct validity verified through factor loading analysis.\n48\t   - Evidence needed: plan_005, plan_006\n49\t\n50\t5. **\"RL robustness is only theoretical — where's the empirical evidence?\"**\n51\t   - Response: plan_002 directly evaluates DIF on cohorts including RL-trained models.\n52\t   - Evidence needed: plan_002\n53\t\n54\t6. **\"Computational cost of the full pipeline\"**\n55\t   - Response: DIF analysis is lightweight (minutes, CPU only). Main cost is one-time calibration panel. Once calibrated, ongoing monitoring is cheap.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e9524a6-c1ea-4d71-a0f5-7ae7328ccf37","uuid":"f776238e-adf6-4560-8291-2341093bc73e","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:08:08.112Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T194223/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: ICLR 2027 (expected deadline ~October 2026; 5 months for full pipeline experiments)\n- Backup: AAAI 2027 (abstract July 21, paper July 28, 2026 — tight, 2 months)\n- Backup 2: EACL 2027 via ARR August 2026 cycle (August 3, 2026)\n\n## Core Claims (3 条, 可证伪)\n\n**Claim 1 (Detection)**: DIF analysis across model release cohorts detects benchmark contamination with practical power (ETS C: TPR 0.72-0.85, FPR <0.05 at N≥80, δ≥1.4) and is robust to RL training — because it operates on group-level behavioral response patterns (correct/incorrect conditional on ability), not within-model output distributions that GRPO/PPO smoothing affects.\n\n**Claim 2 (Ensemble Coverage)**: A multi-signal contamination sentinel combining DIF (large effects, RL-robust), ConStat-style perturbation testing (non-RL models), and DVD generation variance (variant contamination) achieves detection coverage across the full effect-size spectrum and model-type landscape, with each signal covering the blind spots of the others.\n\n**Claim 3 (Regeneration)**: Bifactor IRT equating with anchor items enables psychometrically equivalent benchmark regeneration — flagged items can be replaced with empirically calibrated alternatives that preserve construct validity, difficulty, and discrimination, maintaining benchmark comparability through a formal graceful-degradation framework.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n**Problem**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent ability. Contamination systematically erodes this validity. Critically, RL training (GRPO/PPO) conceals contamination signals: Wang et al. (ICLR 2026) show 14-20pp AUROC degradation for all reference-free detectors after ~156 GRPO steps, reducing most to near-random (~50% AUROC). The model ecosystem is shifting toward RL-trained reasoning models (o1, o3, DeepSeek-R1), making this a growing threat.\n\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: LiveBench updates monthly from recent sources but applies no psychometric calibration across updates. ConStat provides FDR-controlled performance-based detection but relies on perturbation sensitivity that RL can mask. DVD detects variant contamination via generation variance but is untested against RL. Growing Pains (arXiv 2026) uses multidimensional IRT for extensible evaluation but addresses score comparability, not contamination. No existing work closes the full loop from RL-robust detection through construct-constrained generation to psychometrically equated regeneration.\n\n**Our framing**: Contamination is fundamentally a psychometric problem — it creates Differential Item Functioning (DIF), where contaminated items become differentially easier for exposed model cohorts beyond what general ability gains predict. DIF operates on group-level Item Characteristic Curves conditional on ability, making it orthogonal to within-model output distribution smoothing. This is the one contamination signal RL cannot conceal without negating the purpose of contamination itself: if a model memorized an item, it must answer it correctly, creating a detectable behavioral anomaly at the population level. Combined with a multi-signal ensemble for full effect-size coverage and bifactor IRT equating for calibrated item regeneration, this creates the first self-healing benchmark framework.\n\n**Headline result template**: \"On MMLU with 5,000+ models spanning 3 years of releases, DIF-based ETS C detection achieves 73-85% TPR with <5% FPR for large contamination effects (δ≥1.4), maintaining power where 10 existing detection methods degrade to near-random under RL training (Wang et al., ICLR 2026).\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **ICLR**: Strong fit — evaluation methodology, robustness to RL, psychometric theory applied to ML. Risk: reviewers may not be familiar with IRT/DIF methodology. Mitigation: provide self-contained DIF tutorial in appendix, reproducible code, and connection to ML-familiar concepts (DIF ≈ \"fairness testing for items\").\n- **Cross-discipline bridge**: IRT/psychometrics vocabulary needs translation for ML audience. Key mappings: \"examinees\" → \"models\", \"test items\" → \"benchmark questions\", \"DIF\" → \"item-level contamination signal\", \"equating\" → \"score comparability across benchmark versions\".\n- **Novelty concern**: DIF itself is not new (1988). Our contribution is the novel application to LLM benchmark contamination + the RL-robustness argument + the integration with regeneration. Need to frame as \"bringing mature psychometric tools to solve an urgent ML problem\" rather than \"inventing new statistics.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects (δ≥1.4)\"**\n   - Response: Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most (GSM1K: 10-13% average accuracy drop). Small effects (δ<0.6) have minimal impact on rankings. For medium effects, the ensemble's other signals provide coverage.\n   - Evidence needed: plan_001 (real-data validation), plan_003 (ensemble)\n\n2. **\"Model cohort sample sizes are too small for classical DIF\"**\n   - Response: (a) ETS C uses effect-size thresholds, not p-values, reducing sample-size dependence; (b) annual cohorts now reach N=80-100; (c) Cumulative Bayesian priors accumulate power over time; (d) Item-Focused Trees treat release date as continuous covariate.\n   - Evidence needed: plan_001 (real cohort sizes), plan_008 (Bayesian DIF, P2)\n\n3. **\"Only validated in simulation\"**\n   - Response: plan_001 uses METABENCH real data (5,055 models). plan_004 cross-validates on GSM8K with GSM1K ground truth.\n   - Evidence needed: plan_001, plan_004\n\n4. **\"Item regeneration quality — how do you ensure replacements measure the same construct?\"**\n   - Response: Bifactor IRT equating with anchor items + empirical calibration via student simulation (not prompt-based difficulty targeting). Construct validity verified through factor loading analysis.\n   - Evidence needed: plan_005, plan_006\n\n5. **\"RL robustness is only theoretical — where's the empirical evidence?\"**\n   - Response: plan_002 directly evaluates DIF on cohorts including RL-trained models.\n   - Evidence needed: plan_002\n\n6. **\"Computational cost of the full pipeline\"**\n   - Response: DIF analysis is lightweight (minutes, CPU only). Main cost is one-time calibration panel. Once calibrated, ongoing monitoring is cheap.\n","numLines":56,"startLine":1,"totalLines":56}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011E4kattbq91SsxUmyD9Fth","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"对METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,055 models × 12,508 items)执行temporal cohort DIF分析， 以MMLU-CF为partial ground truth验证。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"dif_tpr_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.38,\n7\t      \"dif_tpr_delta_ge_1.0\": 0.18,\n8\t      \"dif_fpr\": 0.12,\n9\t      \"mmlu_cf_correlation_with_dif_flags_phi\": 0.09,\n10\t      \"mmlu_cf_correlation_with_dif_flags_spearman\": 0.07,\n11\t      \"irt_model_fit_rmsea\": 0.11,\n12\t      \"irt_model_fit_cfi\": 0.78,\n13\t      \"n_items_flagged_ets_c\": 1840,\n14\t      \"n_items_flagged_ets_c_after_fpr_correction\": 620,\n15\t      \"cohort_size_pre2024\": 1850,\n16\t      \"cohort_size_post2024\": 3205,\n17\t      \"unidimensionality_test_p\": 0.001,\n18\t      \"item_discrimination_variance\": 2.8\n19\t    },\n20\t    \"tables\": [\n21\t      {\n22\t        \"title\": \"Table 1: DIF Detection Performance on METABENCH MMLU (Worst Tier)\",\n23\t        \"columns\": [\n24\t          \"metric\",\n25\t          \"pre2024_vs_post2024\",\n26\t          \"annual_cohorts\",\n27\t          \"sliding_window_6mo\"\n28\t        ],\n29\t        \"rows\": [\n30\t          [\n31\t            \"TPR_delta_ge_1.4\",\n32\t            0.38,\n33\t            0.31,\n34\t            0.28\n35\t          ],\n36\t          [\n37\t            \"TPR_delta_ge_1.0\",\n38\t            0.18,\n39\t            0.14,\n40\t            0.12\n41\t          ],\n42\t          [\n43\t            \"FPR\",\n44\t            0.12,\n45\t            0.14,\n46\t            0.15\n47\t          ],\n48\t          [\n49\t            \"F1_delta_ge_1.4\",\n50\t            0.33,\n51\t            0.28,\n52\t            0.25\n53\t          ],\n54\t          [\n55\t            \"N_flagged_items\",\n56\t            1840,\n57\t            2100,\n58\t            2350\n59\t          ],\n60\t          [\n61\t            \"MMLU-CF_phi_correlation\",\n62\t            0.09,\n63\t            0.07,\n64\t            0.06\n65\t          ]\n66\t        ]\n67\t      },\n68\t      {\n69\t        \"title\": \"Table 2: IRT Model Fit Diagnostics\",\n70\t        \"columns\": [\n71\t          \"fit_index\",\n72\t          \"value\",\n73\t          \"acceptable_threshold\",\n74\t          \"verdict\"\n75\t        ],\n76\t        \"rows\": [\n77\t          [\n78\t            \"RMSEA\",\n79\t            0.11,\n80\t            \"≤0.06\",\n81\t            \"FAIL\"\n82\t          ],\n83\t          [\n84\t            \"CFI\",\n85\t            0.78,\n86\t            \"≥0.90\",\n87\t            \"FAIL\"\n88\t          ],\n89\t          [\n90\t            \"TLI\",\n91\t            0.74,\n92\t            \"≥0.90\",\n93\t            \"FAIL\"\n94\t          ],\n95\t          [\n96\t            \"SRMR\",\n97\t            0.09,\n98\t            \"≤0.08\",\n99\t            \"FAIL\"\n100\t          ],\n101\t          [\n102\t            \"M2_p_value\",\n103\t            \"<0.001\",\n104\t            \">0.05\",\n105\t            \"FAIL\"\n106\t          ]\n107\t        ]\n108\t      }\n109\t    ],\n110\t    \"figures\": [],\n111\t    \"analysis\": \"核心发现：real data上IRT model严重misfit，DIF检测被architecture heterogeneity主导。 Simulation中（Phase 2, N=100, δ=1.4, TPR=0.76）的performance无法迁移到real data， 因为simulation假设了unidimensional ability和homogeneous population——这在5055个异构模型上 完全不成立。FPR=0.12意味着每1000个clean items中有120个被错误flagged，在MMLU的12508个items 上产生约1500个false positives，淹没了真正的contamination signal。MMLU-CF validation几乎 为negative（phi=0.09），无法作为DIF有效性的支撑证据。结论：categorical temporal cohort DIF 在heterogeneous model population上不可直接使用。\\n\\n\\n5055个模型跨越encoder-only (BERT-family)、decoder-only (GPT/LLaMA family)、MoE等根本不同 的architecture，对MMLU items的response pattern受architecture驱动而非ability驱动。例如 decoder-only模型在long-context reasoning items上系统性优于encoder-only模型，这与contamination 无关但产生大量DIF。RMSEA=0.11远超可接受阈值(0.06)，CFI=0.78低于0.90标准，表明unidimensional IRT model严重misfit。在此背景下ETS C的effect-size threshold无法区分architecture-driven DIF 和contamination-driven DIF，导致FPR膨胀至0.12。1840个items被flagged（15%的item pool）， 其中大部分是false positives。与MMLU-CF的correlation仅phi=0.09，接近random——因为MMLU-CF 本身的contamination annotation也有噪声（它只标注了\\\"显著修改\\\"的items，但并未验证原始items 确实被contaminated），加上DIF flags被spurious signal淹没，两个noisy signal之间几乎无相关。\\n\"\n112\t  },\n113\t  {\n114\t    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n115\t    \"description\": \"对比DIF与传统检测器在包含/不包含RL-trained模型的cohort上的表现差异。\\n\",\n116\t    \"results\": {\n117\t      \"dif_tpr_sft_only_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.42,\n118\t      \"dif_tpr_with_rl_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.29,\n119\t      \"dif_power_retention_ratio\": 0.69,\n120\t      \"traditional_mink_auroc_sft\": 0.74,\n121\t      \"traditional_mink_auroc_rl\": 0.58,\n122\t      \"traditional_constat_auroc_sft\": 0.71,\n123\t      \"traditional_constat_auroc_rl\": 0.61,\n124\t      \"traditional_dvd_auroc_sft\": 0.68,\n125\t      \"traditional_dvd_auroc_rl\": 0.55,\n126\t      \"dif_auroc_sft\": 0.67,\n127\t      \"dif_auroc_rl\": 0.54,\n128\t      \"dif_vs_traditional_auroc_gap_under_rl\": 0.02,\n129\t      \"n_rl_models_available\": 12,\n130\t      \"rl_model_cohort_size\": 12\n131\t    },\n132\t    \"tables\": [\n133\t      {\n134\t        \"title\": \"Table 3: RL-Robustness Comparison — DIF vs Traditional Detectors\",\n135\t        \"columns\": [\n136\t          \"method\",\n137\t          \"auroc_sft_cohort\",\n138\t          \"auroc_rl_cohort\",\n139\t          \"retention_ratio\",\n140\t          \"delta_auroc\"\n141\t        ],\n142\t        \"rows\": [\n143\t          [\n144\t            \"DIF_ETS_C\",\n145\t            0.67,\n146\t            0.54,\n147\t            0.81,\n148\t            -0.13\n149\t          ],\n150\t          [\n151\t            \"Min-K%\",\n152\t            0.74,\n153\t            0.58,\n154\t            0.78,\n155\t            -0.16\n156\t          ],\n157\t          [\n158\t            \"ConStat\",\n159\t            0.71,\n160\t            0.61,\n161\t            0.86,\n162\t            -0.1\n163\t          ],\n164\t          [\n165\t            \"DVD\",\n166\t            0.68,\n167\t            0.55,\n168\t            0.81,\n169\t            -0.13\n170\t          ],\n171\t          [\n172\t            \"Perplexity\",\n173\t            0.69,\n174\t            0.56,\n175\t            0.81,\n176\t            -0.13\n177\t          ]\n178\t        ]\n179\t      },\n180\t      {\n181\t        \"title\": \"Table 4: DIF TPR Under SFT vs RL Cohorts\",\n182\t        \"columns\": [\n183\t          \"effect_size\",\n184\t          \"tpr_sft_only\",\n185\t          \"tpr_with_rl\",\n186\t          \"retention\"\n187\t        ],\n188\t        \"rows\": [\n189\t          [\n190\t            \"δ≥1.6\",\n191\t            0.48,\n192\t            0.35,\n193\t            0.73\n194\t          ],\n195\t          [\n196\t            \"δ≥1.4\",\n197\t            0.42,\n198\t            0.29,\n199\t            0.69\n200\t          ],\n201\t          [\n202\t            \"δ≥1.0\",\n203\t            0.2,\n204\t            0.13,\n205\t            0.65\n206\t          ],\n207\t          [\n208\t            \"δ≥0.6\",\n209\t            0.09,\n210\t            0.06,\n211\t            0.67\n212\t          ]\n213\t        ]\n214\t      }\n215\t    ],\n216\t    \"figures\": [],\n217\t    \"analysis\": \"DIF的RL-robustness优势不显著。AUROC under RL: DIF 0.54 vs best traditional 0.61 (ConStat)， DIF实际上略差于ConStat。Power retention ratio 0.69落在worst tier预测范围[0.5, 0.75]内。 核心问题：RL改变ICC形状（discrimination parameter a也变化），不仅仅是difficulty shift， 这意味着DIF的理论robustness argument不成立。加上RL cohort sample size仅12，统计结论的 可靠性本身存疑。无法支撑paper的headline claim。\\n\\n\\nRL-robustness假设的理论基础是\\\"DIF操作在group-level ICC上，RL只平移不改变ICC形状\\\"。但worst 情景下RL不仅平移ICC——GRPO/PPO通过reward shaping改变了模型在不同difficulty levels上的response pattern，导致ICC形状本身变化（slope变陡或变平）。这使得RL-trained模型与SFT模型之间的ICC差异 既来自contamination也来自training method，DIF无法区分二者。DIF在RL cohort下power从0.42降到 0.29（retention ratio=0.69），传统方法从~0.71降到~0.58。关键是DIF的降幅比例与传统方法相当， AUROC差距仅0.02——不足以支撑\\\"DIF是RL-orthogonal signal\\\"的核心论点。此外，可获取的RL模型 仅12个（METABENCH中标注为RL-trained的开源模型有限），cohort太小导致DIF统计功效本身就低， 难以将power loss归因于RL vs simply small N。\\n\"\n218\t  },\n219\t  {\n220\t    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n221\t    \"description\": \"独立评估ConStat-style perturbation testing在MMLU上的contamination检测能力。\\n\",\n222\t    \"results\": {\n223\t      \"constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_0.6\": 0.32,\n224\t      \"constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_1.0\": 0.45,\n225\t      \"constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.55,\n226\t      \"constat_tpr_rl_delta_ge_0.6\": 0.11,\n227\t      \"constat_tpr_rl_delta_ge_1.0\": 0.18,\n228\t      \"constat_fpr\": 0.06,\n229\t      \"constat_fdr_controlled_power\": 0.28,\n230\t      \"n_perturbation_items_generated\": 220,\n231\t      \"perturbation_quality_human_equiv_rate\": 0.82,\n232\t      \"paraphrase_semantic_similarity\": 0.91\n233\t    },\n234\t    \"tables\": [\n235\t      {\n236\t        \"title\": \"Table 5: ConStat Perturbation Detection by Effect Size and Model Type\",\n237\t        \"columns\": [\n238\t          \"effect_size\",\n239\t          \"tpr_sft\",\n240\t          \"tpr_rl\",\n241\t          \"tpr_mixed\",\n242\t          \"fpr\"\n243\t        ],\n244\t        \"rows\": [\n245\t          [\n246\t            \"δ≥1.4\",\n247\t            0.55,\n248\t            0.18,\n249\t            0.38,\n250\t            0.06\n251\t          ],\n252\t          [\n253\t            \"δ≥1.0\",\n254\t            0.45,\n255\t            0.14,\n256\t            0.3,\n257\t            0.06\n258\t          ],\n259\t          [\n260\t            \"δ≥0.6\",\n261\t            0.32,\n262\t            0.11,\n263\t            0.22,\n264\t            0.07\n265\t          ],\n266\t          [\n267\t            \"δ≥0.4\",\n268\t            0.19,\n269\t            0.08,\n270\t            0.14,\n271\t            0.07\n272\t          ]\n273\t        ]\n274\t      }\n275\t    ],\n276\t    \"figures\": [],\n277\t    \"analysis\": \"ConStat在non-RL场景下对large effects有moderate power，但RL场景下急剧退化。作为ensemble component对non-RL覆盖有限值，但无法作为RL-robust complement to DIF（两者在RL下都弱）。 FDR-controlled power 0.28意味着实际可用的detection capacity很有限。\\n\\n\\nConStat在non-RL模型上有中等检测力（TPR=0.32 for δ≥0.6），因为SFT模型对verbatim memorized items的perturbation确实敏感——答对原题但答错改写题是contamination的合理信号。 但在worst tier下：(1) 真实contamination多为partial memorization，模型可能只记住了answer pattern而非exact wording，对perturbation同样答对，降低sensitivity；(2) LLM paraphrase 生成的reformulations质量参差——82%被判为semantically equivalent，但18%引入了微妙的 difficulty变化，增加noise；(3) RL模型对perturbation的sensitivity本身就低（RL鼓励 generalization），RL场景下TPR骤降至0.11。FDR-controlled power仅0.28，意味着在控制 false discovery rate后，能检出的contaminated items不到三分之一。作为standalone result 有一定baseline价值，但不足以独立成章。\\n\"\n278\t  },\n279\t  {\n280\t    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n281\t    \"description\": \"独立评估DVD generation variance方法在MMLU上检测variant contamination的能力。\\n\",\n282\t    \"results\": {\n283\t      \"dvd_tpr_variant_contamination\": 0.22,\n284\t      \"dvd_tpr_verbatim_contamination\": 0.48,\n285\t      \"dvd_tpr_partial_contamination\": 0.12,\n286\t      \"dvd_fpr\": 0.09,\n287\t      \"dvd_auroc_overall\": 0.61,\n288\t      \"n_models_evaluated\": 13,\n289\t      \"n_items_sampled\": 500,\n290\t      \"responses_per_item\": 50,\n291\t      \"bimodal_distribution_rate_contaminated\": 0.18,\n292\t      \"bimodal_distribution_rate_clean\": 0.07,\n293\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 65\n294\t    },\n295\t    \"tables\": [\n296\t      {\n297\t        \"title\": \"Table 6: DVD Detection by Contamination Type\",\n298\t        \"columns\": [\n299\t          \"contamination_type\",\n300\t          \"tpr\",\n301\t          \"fpr\",\n302\t          \"auroc\",\n303\t          \"n_items\"\n304\t        ],\n305\t        \"rows\": [\n306\t          [\n307\t            \"verbatim\",\n308\t            0.48,\n309\t            0.09,\n310\t            0.72,\n311\t            120\n312\t          ],\n313\t          [\n314\t            \"variant\",\n315\t            0.22,\n316\t            0.09,\n317\t            0.58,\n318\t            180\n319\t          ],\n320\t          [\n321\t            \"partial\",\n322\t            0.12,\n323\t            0.09,\n324\t            0.52,\n325\t            200\n326\t          ],\n327\t          [\n328\t            \"overall\",\n329\t            0.25,\n330\t            0.09,\n331\t            0.61,\n332\t            500\n333\t          ]\n334\t        ]\n335\t      }\n336\t    ],\n337\t    \"figures\": [],\n338\t    \"analysis\": \"DVD对variant contamination的检测力远低于预期（TPR=0.22 vs 论文claim需要的高coverage）。 核心问题是real-world contamination不产生clean bimodal response pattern——partial memorization 导致diffuse variance而非bimodal variance。GPU开销大但回报低，作为ensemble component 贡献有限。\\n\\n\\nDVD的理论基础是contaminated items上model generation variance呈bimodal分布（有时recall memorized answer，有时不能）。在worst tier下：(1) variant contamination（题目被改写后 contaminated）信号最弱——模型对variant的memorization不稳定，generation variance与clean items差异小，TPR仅0.22；(2) partial contamination（仅记住部分信息）几乎无法检测（TPR=0.12）， 因为partial memory不产生bimodal response pattern，而是持续的uncertainty；(3) 即使verbatim contamination，TPR也仅0.48，因为很多模型在temperature sampling下对已知答案也表现stable （always correct），generation variance反而很低——与clean but easy items难以区分；(4) bimodal rate在contaminated items上仅18% vs clean items 7%，差异有统计显著性但effect size 太小无法做reliable detection。FPR=0.09偏高。总计消耗65 GPU hours，性价比低。\\n\"\n339\t  },\n340\t  {\n341\t    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n342\t    \"description\": \"将DIF + ConStat + DVD融合为多信号ensemble，评估覆盖度和precision。\\n\",\n343\t    \"results\": {\n344\t      \"ensemble_tpr_full_spectrum\": 0.42,\n345\t      \"ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.52,\n346\t      \"ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_1.0\": 0.3,\n347\t      \"ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_0.6\": 0.18,\n348\t      \"ensemble_fpr\": 0.11,\n349\t      \"ensemble_f1\": 0.35,\n350\t      \"majority_voting_tpr\": 0.38,\n351\t      \"weighted_fusion_tpr\": 0.42,\n352\t      \"signal_correlation_dif_constat\": 0.61,\n353\t      \"signal_correlation_dif_dvd\": 0.54,\n354\t      \"signal_correlation_constat_dvd\": 0.58,\n355\t      \"unique_items_flagged_by_only_one_signal_pct\": 0.15,\n356\t      \"items_flagged_by_all_three_pct\": 0.42\n357\t    },\n358\t    \"tables\": [\n359\t      {\n360\t        \"title\": \"Table 7: Ensemble vs Individual Signal Performance\",\n361\t        \"columns\": [\n362\t          \"method\",\n363\t          \"tpr_ge_1.4\",\n364\t          \"tpr_ge_1.0\",\n365\t          \"tpr_ge_0.6\",\n366\t          \"fpr\",\n367\t          \"f1\"\n368\t        ],\n369\t        \"rows\": [\n370\t          [\n371\t            \"DIF_only\",\n372\t            0.38,\n373\t            0.18,\n374\t            0.09,\n375\t            0.12,\n376\t            0.25\n377\t          ],\n378\t          [\n379\t            \"ConStat_only\",\n380\t            0.38,\n381\t            0.3,\n382\t            0.22,\n383\t            0.06,\n384\t            0.32\n385\t          ],\n386\t          [\n387\t            \"DVD_only\",\n388\t            0.25,\n389\t            0.15,\n390\t            0.1,\n391\t            0.09,\n392\t            0.18\n393\t          ],\n394\t          [\n395\t            \"Majority_2of3\",\n396\t            0.38,\n397\t            0.19,\n398\t            0.11,\n399\t            0.05,\n400\t            0.3\n401\t          ],\n402\t          [\n403\t            \"Weighted_fusion\",\n404\t            0.52,\n405\t            0.3,\n406\t            0.18,\n407\t            0.11,\n408\t            0.35\n409\t          ]\n410\t        ]\n411\t      },\n412\t      {\n413\t        \"title\": \"Table 8: Signal Correlation Matrix\",\n414\t        \"columns\": [\n415\t          \"signal_pair\",\n416\t          \"pearson_r\",\n417\t          \"overlap_in_flagged_items_pct\"\n418\t        ],\n419\t        \"rows\": [\n420\t          [\n421\t            \"DIF-ConStat\",\n422\t            0.61,\n423\t            0.68\n424\t          ],\n425\t          [\n426\t            \"DIF-DVD\",\n427\t            0.54,\n428\t            0.59\n429\t          ],\n430\t          [\n431\t            \"ConStat-DVD\",\n432\t            0.58,\n433\t            0.63\n434\t          ]\n435\t        ]\n436\t      }\n437\t    ],\n438\t    \"figures\": [],\n439\t    \"analysis\": \"Ensemble的\\\"互补覆盖\\\"核心假设不成立。信号间高相关（0.54-0.61）意味着ensemble主要在置信度上 提升（对已检出items更confident）而非在覆盖度上提升（检出新items）。Weighted fusion的TPR=0.42 仅比best individual signal (ConStat 0.30 at δ≥1.0) 提升有限，且FPR=0.11偏高。这个ensemble 不能作为\\\"full-spectrum detection system\\\"呈现——更准确的描述是\\\"three weak signals with correlated failure modes\\\"。\\n\\n\\nEnsemble假设三个signal互补——DIF覆盖large effects+RL场景，ConStat覆盖non-RL medium effects， DVD覆盖variant contamination。但worst tier下：(1) 三个signal之间correlation高（r=0.54-0.61）， 表明它们largely flag同一批items而非互补覆盖不同盲区；(2) 仅15%的items被unique地由某一个 signal单独检出，说明\\\"互补覆盖\\\"理论不成立——各signal的failure modes相关（都在partial/medium effect上失败）；(3) 42%的items被三个signal同时flag，说明easy cases三者都能检出但hard cases 三者都漏检；(4) FPR=0.11，majority voting无法有效压低FPR因为false positives也呈相关模式 （architecture-driven spurious DIF也往往在perturbation testing中产生false positive）。 Weighted fusion比majority voting略好（TPR 0.42 vs 0.38）但提升有限。整体full-spectrum TPR=0.42落在worst tier [0.35, 0.6]范围内，不足以作为实用detection system。\\n\"\n440\t  },\n441\t  {\n442\t    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n443\t    \"description\": \"在GSM8K上复制DIF分析，以GSM1K作为contamination ground truth进行交叉验证。\\n\",\n444\t    \"results\": {\n445\t      \"gsm8k_gsm1k_gap_dif_correlation_spearman\": 0.11,\n446\t      \"gsm8k_gsm1k_gap_dif_correlation_pearson\": 0.08,\n447\t      \"dif_tpr_gsm8k_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.3,\n448\t      \"dif_fpr_gsm8k\": 0.13,\n449\t      \"n_models_with_both_gsm8k_gsm1k\": 48,\n450\t      \"irt_model_fit_rmsea_gsm8k\": 0.09,\n451\t      \"gsm8k_item_discrimination_mean\": 0.85,\n452\t      \"gsm1k_gap_mean_across_models\": 0.07,\n453\t      \"gsm1k_gap_std\": 0.11,\n454\t      \"n_items_gsm8k_analyzed\": 1319\n455\t    },\n456\t    \"tables\": [\n457\t      {\n458\t        \"title\": \"Table 9: GSM8K Cross-Validation Results\",\n459\t        \"columns\": [\n460\t          \"metric\",\n461\t          \"value\",\n462\t          \"worst_tier_range\",\n463\t          \"verdict\"\n464\t        ],\n465\t        \"rows\": [\n466\t          [\n467\t            \"DIF_TPR_δ≥1.4\",\n468\t            0.3,\n469\t            \"0.25-0.50\",\n470\t            \"IN_RANGE\"\n471\t          ],\n472\t          [\n473\t            \"DIF_FPR\",\n474\t            0.13,\n475\t            \"0.08-0.15\",\n476\t            \"IN_RANGE\"\n477\t          ],\n478\t          [\n479\t            \"GSM8K-GSM1K_gap_correlation\",\n480\t            0.11,\n481\t            \"0.0-0.18\",\n482\t            \"IN_RANGE\"\n483\t          ],\n484\t          [\n485\t            \"N_models\",\n486\t            48,\n487\t            \"≥50 desired\",\n488\t            \"INSUFFICIENT\"\n489\t          ],\n490\t          [\n491\t            \"IRT_fit_RMSEA\",\n492\t            0.09,\n493\t            \"≤0.06\",\n494\t            \"FAIL\"\n495\t          ]\n496\t        ]\n497\t      }\n498\t    ],\n499\t    \"figures\": [],\n500\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark validation为negative result。GSM8K上DIF表现与MMLU类似（low TPR, high FPR）， 且与GSM1K ground truth的correlation接近零（rho=0.11）。样本量不足（48 models vs desired 50+） 进一步削弱统计结论的可靠性。这不能作为DIF generalizability的支撑证据。\\n\\n\\nGSM8K validation在worst tier下面临多重困难：(1) 可获取的同时有GSM8K和GSM1K结果的模型仅 约48个（远少于MMLU的5055个），DIF统计功效严重不足；(2) GSM8K是math benchmark，item discrimination偏低(mean a=0.85)因为数学题的对错更binary、less informative about latent ability gradient，这直接降低DIF detection power；(3) GSM8K-GSM1K gap本身noisy（std=0.11 vs mean=0.07），gap的model-level variance高说明contamination不是uniform的——不同模型 contamination程度差异大，但DIF是item-level metric，model-level gap与item-level DIF flag之间的mapping本就不是直接对应的；(4) GSM1K作为ground truth的assumption是\\\"GSM1K uncontaminated\\\"，但GSM1K发布后也可能被contaminated，ground truth本身会退化。 Spearman rho=0.11几乎无相关，无法支撑cross-benchmark generalizability。\\n\"\n501\t  },\n502\t  {\n503\t    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n504\t    \"description\": \"在METABENCH MMLU数据上拟合bifactor IRT模型，选取anchor items，执行equating pilot。\\n\",\n505\t    \"results\": {\n506\t      \"bifactor_convergence\": \"partial\",\n507\t      \"bifactor_iterations_to_convergence\": 8500,\n508\t      \"bifactor_n_items_converged\": 9200,\n509\t      \"bifactor_n_items_failed\": 3308,\n510\t      \"general_factor_variance_explained\": 0.35,\n511\t      \"n_specific_factors\": 57,\n512\t      \"specific_factor_avg_loading\": 0.28,\n513\t      \"anchor_item_n_selected\": 380,\n514\t      \"anchor_item_stability_mean_dif\": 0.15,\n515\t      \"equating_spearman_rho_before\": 0.82,\n516\t      \"equating_spearman_rho_after\": 0.85,\n517\t      \"equating_rank_displacement_mean\": 3.2,\n518\t      \"equating_rank_displacement_p95\": 12,\n519\t      \"score_reliability_original\": 0.94,\n520\t      \"score_reliability_equated\": 0.89\n521\t    },\n522\t    \"tables\": [\n523\t      {\n524\t        \"title\": \"Table 10: Bifactor IRT Model Fit and Equating Results\",\n525\t        \"columns\": [\n526\t          \"metric\",\n527\t          \"value\",\n528\t          \"target\",\n529\t          \"verdict\"\n530\t        ],\n531\t        \"rows\": [\n532\t          [\n533\t            \"convergence_rate\",\n534\t            \"73.5%\",\n535\t            \"≥95%\",\n536\t            \"FAIL\"\n537\t          ],\n538\t          [\n539\t            \"general_factor_variance\",\n540\t            0.35,\n541\t            \"≥0.50\",\n542\t            \"WEAK\"\n543\t          ],\n544\t          [\n545\t            \"anchor_items_available\",\n546\t            380,\n547\t            \"≥500\",\n548\t            \"MARGINAL\"\n549\t          ],\n550\t          [\n551\t            \"equating_rho\",\n552\t            0.85,\n553\t            \"≥0.95\",\n554\t            \"FAIL\"\n555\t          ],\n556\t          [\n557\t            \"rank_displacement_p95\",\n558\t            12,\n559\t            \"≤5\",\n560\t            \"FAIL\"\n561\t          ],\n562\t          [\n563\t            \"score_reliability_post\",\n564\t            0.89,\n565\t            \"≥0.92\",\n566\t            \"MARGINAL\"\n567\t          ]\n568\t        ]\n569\t      },\n570\t      {\n571\t        \"title\": \"Table 11: Factor Structure Summary\",\n572\t        \"columns\": [\n573\t          \"factor_type\",\n574\t          \"n_factors\",\n575\t          \"mean_loading\",\n576\t          \"pct_items_loading_gt_0.3\"\n577\t        ],\n578\t        \"rows\": [\n579\t          [\n580\t            \"general\",\n581\t            1,\n582\t            0.42,\n583\t            \"62%\"\n584\t          ],\n585\t          [\n586\t            \"specific_STEM\",\n587\t            14,\n588\t            0.31,\n589\t            \"38%\"\n590\t          ],\n591\t          [\n592\t            \"specific_humanities\",\n593\t            18,\n594\t            0.26,\n595\t            \"29%\"\n596\t          ],\n597\t          [\n598\t            \"specific_social_science\",\n599\t            15,\n600\t            0.28,\n601\t            \"33%\"\n602\t          ],\n603\t          [\n604\t            \"specific_other\",\n605\t            10,\n606\t            0.24,\n607\t            \"25%\"\n608\t          ]\n609\t        ]\n610\t      }\n611\t    ],\n612\t    \"figures\": [],\n613\t    \"analysis\": \"Bifactor model在异构LLM population上partially converges但factor structure不清晰。 General factor太弱（35% variance）挑战了\\\"MMLU measures a coherent construct\\\"的前提。 Equating产生了modest improvement (0.82→0.85) 但远未达到psychometric equivalence标准 (0.95)。作为独立贡献（Claim 3 standalone），这个result需要被framed为\\\"benchmark multidimensionality的empirical characterization\\\"而非\\\"successful equating\\\"。可能可以 pivot到Growing Pains style的\\\"LLM evaluation需要multidimensional IRT\\\"叙事。\\n\\n\\nBifactor model在5055个异构模型上面临严重的estimation challenge：(1) 57个MMLU subjects作为 specific factors，加上1个general factor，parameter space巨大（~12500 items × 3 parameters × 58 factors），在worst tier下3308个items（26%）的参数估计不收敛或产生Heywood cases （negative variance estimates）；(2) general factor仅解释35%的variance——这意味着MMLU 不是primarily measuring一个general LLM ability，而是highly multidimensional的，bifactor structure不是good fit；(3) specific factor loadings平均仅0.28，说明subject-level factors 也很弱，很多items不清晰地load在任何factor上——factor structure不可解释；(4) 尽管如此， equating在技术上仍可执行：选出380个stable anchor items（无DIF、参数估计收敛），equating 后ranking correlation从0.82提升到0.85，但这个提升幅度小（Δ=0.03），且基线rho=0.82 已低于Claim 3要求的0.95标准。Equating没有失败但也没有convincingly成功——它能small improvement ranking stability，但不能达到psychometric equivalence的标准。\\n\"\n614\t  },\n615\t  {\n616\t    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n617\t    \"description\": \"生成替代items并通过student simulation进行calibration，评估difficulty estimation质量。\\n\",\n618\t    \"results\": {\n619\t      \"n_items_generated\": 150,\n620\t      \"n_items_passing_quality_filter\": 112,\n621\t      \"difficulty_calibration_rho_student_sim\": 0.48,\n622\t      \"difficulty_calibration_rho_prompt_based\": 0.22,\n623\t      \"difficulty_mae_student_sim\": 0.85,\n624\t      \"difficulty_mae_prompt_based\": 1.45,\n625\t      \"discrimination_calibration_rho\": 0.31,\n626\t      \"construct_alignment_rate\": 0.72,\n627\t      \"holdout_validation_rho\": 0.44,\n628\t      \"student_sim_correlation_with_real_models\": 0.52,\n629\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 180\n630\t    },\n631\t    \"tables\": [\n632\t      {\n633\t        \"title\": \"Table 12: Item Calibration Comparison\",\n634\t        \"columns\": [\n635\t          \"method\",\n636\t          \"difficulty_rho\",\n637\t          \"difficulty_mae\",\n638\t          \"discrimination_rho\",\n639\t          \"construct_alignment\"\n640\t        ],\n641\t        \"rows\": [\n642\t          [\n643\t            \"student_simulation\",\n644\t            0.48,\n645\t            0.85,\n646\t            0.31,\n647\t            \"72%\"\n648\t          ],\n649\t          [\n650\t            \"prompt_based\",\n651\t            0.22,\n652\t            1.45,\n653\t            0.18,\n654\t            \"65%\"\n655\t          ],\n656\t          [\n657\t            \"random_baseline\",\n658\t            0.05,\n659\t            1.8,\n660\t            0.08,\n661\t            \"45%\"\n662\t          ]\n663\t        ]\n664\t      },\n665\t      {\n666\t        \"title\": \"Table 13: Holdout Validation on 30 Models\",\n667\t        \"columns\": [\n668\t          \"metric\",\n669\t          \"student_sim\",\n670\t          \"prompt_based\"\n671\t        ],\n672\t        \"rows\": [\n673\t          [\n674\t            \"difficulty_rank_correlation\",\n675\t            0.44,\n676\t            0.19\n677\t          ],\n678\t          [\n679\t            \"score_equivalence_rho\",\n680\t            0.78,\n681\t            0.68\n682\t          ],\n683\t          [\n684\t            \"ranking_preservation_top10\",\n685\t            \"70%\",\n686\t            \"50%\"\n687\t          ]\n688\t        ]\n689\t      }\n690\t    ],\n691\t    \"figures\": [],\n692\t    \"analysis\": \"Student simulation在MMLU上的calibration quality不足以支撑reliable item replacement。 Difficulty rho=0.48意味着替换后的benchmark与原版在difficulty ordering上只有moderate agreement，不够做psychometric equating。但student sim vs prompt-based的comparison （0.48 vs 0.22）以及failure mode analysis（which subjects/difficulty ranges失败） 仍有独立的文献贡献价值。\\n\\n\\nItem generation在worst tier下的核心问题：(1) Student simulation (arXiv 2601.09953) 的difficulty estimation在MMLU上表现弱于其在其他benchmarks上的reported results——因为 MMLU covers 57 diverse subjects，student simulation的\\\"simulated students\\\"是single LLM 做capability ablation，但不同subject需要不同type的knowledge/reasoning，single-model simulation无法capture this diversity，rho=0.48；(2) Prompt-based difficulty targeting 依然很差（rho=0.22），与文献报告一致；(3) Student simulation比prompt-based好（0.48 vs 0.22） 但absolute accuracy仍不够——difficulty MAE=0.85 logits意味着平均偏差接近1个标准差， 生成的items实际difficulty与target可能差1-2个difficulty band；(4) Discrimination calibration 更差（rho=0.31），因为discrimination是更subtle的item property，依赖于item如何在不同ability levels上区分模型，student simulation几乎无法capture；(5) Construct alignment rate 72% 意味着28%的generated items虽然表面上是同一subject但实际测量的cognitive process不同 （e.g., 要求recall的item被替换为要求reasoning的item）。这些result不支撑\\\"calibrated item regeneration\\\"的claim，但student sim vs prompt-based的comparison本身有文献价值。\\n\"\n693\t  },\n694\t  {\n695\t    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n696\t    \"description\": \"实现cumulative Bayesian DIF priors，模拟4次successive benchmark administrations的power积累。\\n\",\n697\t    \"results\": {\n698\t      \"single_admin_power_delta_1.0\": 0.15,\n699\t      \"cumulative_power_2_admins_delta_1.0\": 0.22,\n700\t      \"cumulative_power_3_admins_delta_1.0\": 0.3,\n701\t      \"cumulative_power_4_admins_delta_1.0\": 0.38,\n702\t      \"single_admin_power_delta_1.4\": 0.35,\n703\t      \"cumulative_power_4_admins_delta_1.4\": 0.55,\n704\t      \"bayesian_fpr_single\": 0.1,\n705\t      \"bayesian_fpr_cumulative_4\": 0.08,\n706\t      \"prior_informativeness_shrinkage\": 0.45\n707\t    },\n708\t    \"tables\": [\n709\t      {\n710\t        \"title\": \"Table 14: Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power Accumulation\",\n711\t        \"columns\": [\n712\t          \"n_administrations\",\n713\t          \"power_delta_1.0\",\n714\t          \"power_delta_1.4\",\n715\t          \"fpr\"\n716\t        ],\n717\t        \"rows\": [\n718\t          [\n719\t            1,\n720\t            0.15,\n721\t            0.35,\n722\t            0.1\n723\t          ],\n724\t          [\n725\t            2,\n726\t            0.22,\n727\t            0.42,\n728\t            0.09\n729\t          ],\n730\t          [\n731\t            3,\n732\t            0.3,\n733\t            0.49,\n734\t            0.09\n735\t          ],\n736\t          [\n737\t            4,\n738\t            0.38,\n739\t            0.55,\n740\t            0.08\n741\t          ]\n742\t        ]\n743\t      }\n744\t    ],\n745\t    \"figures\": [],\n746\t    \"analysis\": \"Cumulative Bayesian approach有边际收益但无法rescue低baseline power。4 admins后power 仅从0.15升至0.38 (δ=1.0)，远低于theoretical 0.70。Population heterogeneity导致prior transfer效率低。作为P2 experiment，结果不改变overall narrative但进一步确认了DIF在 heterogeneous LLM population上的fundamental limitations。\\n\\n\\nBayesian cumulative priors在worst tier下受到两个因素制约：(1) 如果baseline single-admin power已经很低（0.15 for δ=1.0，因为real data上IRT model misfit），那么cumulative evidence accumulation的起点就低——Bayesian updating from a weak prior仍然是weak， 4次admin后仅到0.38（远低于theoretical prediction of 0.70）；(2) Prior informativeness 受model population heterogeneity影响——如果每次administration的model cohort composition 很不同（architecture mix变化），prior从上一admin的posterior transfer不顺畅，shrinkage factor高达0.45（理想应<0.2），意味着prior对posterior的influence被data overwhelm但data 本身noisy。FPR从0.10降至0.08是modest improvement。总体而言，cumulative approach能 提升power但幅度远不如simulated homogeneous scenarios中的预期。\\n\"\n747\t  },\n748\t  {\n749\t    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n750\t    \"description\": \"分析benchmark在progressive item replacement下的validity degradation。\\n\",\n751\t    \"results\": {\n752\t      \"ranking_stability_5pct_replaced\": 0.94,\n753\t      \"ranking_stability_10pct_replaced\": 0.88,\n754\t      \"ranking_stability_20pct_replaced\": 0.79,\n755\t      \"ranking_stability_50pct_replaced\": 0.62,\n756\t      \"score_reliability_5pct\": 0.92,\n757\t      \"score_reliability_10pct\": 0.88,\n758\t      \"score_reliability_20pct\": 0.81,\n759\t      \"score_reliability_50pct\": 0.67,\n760\t      \"construct_coverage_5pct\": 0.97,\n761\t      \"construct_coverage_10pct\": 0.93,\n762\t      \"construct_coverage_20pct\": 0.85,\n763\t      \"construct_coverage_50pct\": 0.71,\n764\t      \"critical_replacement_threshold\": 0.12\n765\t    },\n766\t    \"tables\": [\n767\t      {\n768\t        \"title\": \"Table 15: Validity Degradation Under Progressive Replacement\",\n769\t        \"columns\": [\n770\t          \"replacement_pct\",\n771\t          \"ranking_rho\",\n772\t          \"reliability\",\n773\t          \"construct_coverage\"\n774\t        ],\n775\t        \"rows\": [\n776\t          [\n777\t            \"0% (baseline)\",\n778\t            1.0,\n779\t            0.94,\n780\t            1.0\n781\t          ],\n782\t          [\n783\t            \"5%\",\n784\t            0.94,\n785\t            0.92,\n786\t            0.97\n787\t          ],\n788\t          [\n789\t            \"10%\",\n790\t            0.88,\n791\t            0.88,\n792\t            0.93\n793\t          ],\n794\t          [\n795\t            \"20%\",\n796\t            0.79,\n797\t            0.81,\n798\t            0.85\n799\t          ],\n800\t          [\n801\t            \"50%\",\n802\t            0.62,\n803\t            0.67,\n804\t            0.71\n805\t          ]\n806\t        ]\n807\t      },\n808\t      {\n809\t        \"title\": \"Table 16: Critical Thresholds\",\n810\t        \"columns\": [\n811\t          \"validity_criterion\",\n812\t          \"threshold_value\",\n813\t          \"max_safe_replacement_pct\"\n814\t        ],\n815\t        \"rows\": [\n816\t          [\n817\t            \"ranking_rho_≥0.90\",\n818\t            0.9,\n819\t            \"12%\"\n820\t          ],\n821\t          [\n822\t            \"reliability_≥0.90\",\n823\t            0.9,\n824\t            \"7%\"\n825\t          ],\n826\t          [\n827\t            \"construct_coverage_≥0.90\",\n828\t            0.9,\n829\t            \"14%\"\n830\t          ],\n831\t          [\n832\t            \"all_criteria_met\",\n833\t            \"-\",\n834\t            \"7%\"\n835\t          ]\n836\t        ]\n837\t      }\n838\t    ],\n839\t    \"figures\": [],\n840\t    \"analysis\": \"Graceful degradation analysis表明在当前calibration quality下，只能安全替换7%的items （约875个items，满足所有validity criteria）。这远不足以构成practical \\\"self-healing\\\" benchmark——如果检测到的contaminated items超过7%，replacement会损害benchmark validity。 这是对Claim 3的严重限制，但degradation curve本身是有价值的empirical contribution， 可以frame为\\\"item replacement的practical bounds\\\"。\\n\\n\\nGraceful degradation在worst tier下退化快于预期因为：(1) Item calibration quality差 （difficulty rho=0.48 from plan_006），替换items的psychometric properties与被替换items 不匹配，每次替换引入的error大于calibration error budget允许的范围；(2) Bifactor equating 不充分（rho=0.85 from plan_005），equating本身引入systematic bias，累积到20%替换时 ranking stability降至0.79（如果equating完美，应维持在0.92+）；(3) Construct coverage degradation因为28%的generated items construct alignment有问题（from plan_006）， 20%替换时约5-6%的items测量不同construct，coverage降至0.85。Critical threshold（ranking rho降至0.90以下的替换比例）仅12%——意味着实际上只能安全替换约1500个items，远少于 potential contaminated items的数量（如果FPR=0.12则约1800个被flag）。\\n\"\n841\t  },\n842\t  {\n843\t    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n844\t    \"description\": \"实现Item-Focused Trees，将model release date作为continuous covariate替代categorical cohort DIF。\\n\",\n845\t    \"results\": {\n846\t      \"ift_tpr_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.33,\n847\t      \"ift_tpr_delta_ge_1.0\": 0.16,\n848\t      \"ift_fpr\": 0.1,\n849\t      \"ift_vs_categorical_dif_tpr_delta\": -0.05,\n850\t      \"ift_computation_time_hours\": 18,\n851\t      \"n_splits_found\": 3.2,\n852\t      \"split_dates_concentration\": \"2023-06 to 2024-01\",\n853\t      \"overfitting_cross_val_tpr_drop\": 0.12\n854\t    },\n855\t    \"tables\": [\n856\t      {\n857\t        \"title\": \"Table 17: Item-Focused Trees vs Categorical DIF\",\n858\t        \"columns\": [\n859\t          \"metric\",\n860\t          \"categorical_dif\",\n861\t          \"ift\",\n862\t          \"delta\"\n863\t        ],\n864\t        \"rows\": [\n865\t          [\n866\t            \"TPR_δ≥1.4\",\n867\t            0.38,\n868\t            0.33,\n869\t            -0.05\n870\t          ],\n871\t          [\n872\t            \"TPR_δ≥1.0\",\n873\t            0.18,\n874\t            0.16,\n875\t            -0.02\n876\t          ],\n877\t          [\n878\t            \"FPR\",\n879\t            0.12,\n880\t            0.1,\n881\t            -0.02\n882\t          ],\n883\t          [\n884\t            \"F1\",\n885\t            0.25,\n886\t            0.24,\n887\t            -0.01\n888\t          ],\n889\t          [\n890\t            \"computation_hours\",\n891\t            0.5,\n892\t            18,\n893\t            \"+17.5\"\n894\t          ]\n895\t        ]\n896\t      }\n897\t    ],\n898\t    \"figures\": [],\n899\t    \"analysis\": \"IFT未能改善DIF detection。Split points与architecture transitions而非contamination events 对齐，进一步证实model heterogeneity是dominant signal source。计算成本高36倍但无performance gain。作为P2 experiment，结论是negative：continuous covariate treatment不解决fundamental 问题。\\n\\nItem-Focused Trees理论上避免arbitrary cohort splits，但在worst tier下：(1) Release date 作为continuous covariate与contamination的关系不是smooth monotonic的——contamination是 event-driven（某次data leak），不是gradual trend，IFT的tree structure可以capture这个 但容易overfit到特定split points；(2) Cross-validation显示TPR drop=0.12，说明overfitting significant；(3) 在model heterogeneity高的情况下，IFT实际上比categorical DIF表现略差 （TPR差-0.05），因为tree splitting在high-noise环境下容易找到spurious splits——3.2个 average splits集中在2023年中到2024年初，这恰好是architecture transition period （GPT-4发布后大量models涌现），tree可能在capture architecture shift而非contamination。 FPR=0.10比categorical DIF（0.12）略低，但improvement不显著。Computation cost 18 hours 因为per-item tree fitting在12508 items上。\\n\"\n900\t  }\n901\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e9524a6-c1ea-4d71-a0f5-7ae7328ccf37","uuid":"85988a30-d737-476d-ac56-52114bcb83dd","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:08:08.288Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T194223/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n    \"description\": \"对METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,055 models × 12,508 items)执行temporal cohort DIF分析， 以MMLU-CF为partial ground truth验证。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dif_tpr_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.38,\n      \"dif_tpr_delta_ge_1.0\": 0.18,\n      \"dif_fpr\": 0.12,\n      \"mmlu_cf_correlation_with_dif_flags_phi\": 0.09,\n      \"mmlu_cf_correlation_with_dif_flags_spearman\": 0.07,\n      \"irt_model_fit_rmsea\": 0.11,\n      \"irt_model_fit_cfi\": 0.78,\n      \"n_items_flagged_ets_c\": 1840,\n      \"n_items_flagged_ets_c_after_fpr_correction\": 620,\n      \"cohort_size_pre2024\": 1850,\n      \"cohort_size_post2024\": 3205,\n      \"unidimensionality_test_p\": 0.001,\n      \"item_discrimination_variance\": 2.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 1: DIF Detection Performance on METABENCH MMLU (Worst Tier)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"pre2024_vs_post2024\",\n          \"annual_cohorts\",\n          \"sliding_window_6mo\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"TPR_delta_ge_1.4\",\n            0.38,\n            0.31,\n            0.28\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TPR_delta_ge_1.0\",\n            0.18,\n            0.14,\n            0.12\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FPR\",\n            0.12,\n            0.14,\n            0.15\n          ],\n          [\n            \"F1_delta_ge_1.4\",\n            0.33,\n            0.28,\n            0.25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"N_flagged_items\",\n            1840,\n            2100,\n            2350\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU-CF_phi_correlation\",\n            0.09,\n            0.07,\n            0.06\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 2: IRT Model Fit Diagnostics\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"fit_index\",\n          \"value\",\n          \"acceptable_threshold\",\n          \"verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RMSEA\",\n            0.11,\n            \"≤0.06\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CFI\",\n            0.78,\n            \"≥0.90\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TLI\",\n            0.74,\n            \"≥0.90\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SRMR\",\n            0.09,\n            \"≤0.08\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"M2_p_value\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \">0.05\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"核心发现：real data上IRT model严重misfit，DIF检测被architecture heterogeneity主导。 Simulation中（Phase 2, N=100, δ=1.4, TPR=0.76）的performance无法迁移到real data， 因为simulation假设了unidimensional ability和homogeneous population——这在5055个异构模型上 完全不成立。FPR=0.12意味着每1000个clean items中有120个被错误flagged，在MMLU的12508个items 上产生约1500个false positives，淹没了真正的contamination signal。MMLU-CF validation几乎 为negative（phi=0.09），无法作为DIF有效性的支撑证据。结论：categorical temporal cohort DIF 在heterogeneous model population上不可直接使用。\\n\\n\\n5055个模型跨越encoder-only (BERT-family)、decoder-only (GPT/LLaMA family)、MoE等根本不同 的architecture，对MMLU items的response pattern受architecture驱动而非ability驱动。例如 decoder-only模型在long-context reasoning items上系统性优于encoder-only模型，这与contamination 无关但产生大量DIF。RMSEA=0.11远超可接受阈值(0.06)，CFI=0.78低于0.90标准，表明unidimensional IRT model严重misfit。在此背景下ETS C的effect-size threshold无法区分architecture-driven DIF 和contamination-driven DIF，导致FPR膨胀至0.12。1840个items被flagged（15%的item pool）， 其中大部分是false positives。与MMLU-CF的correlation仅phi=0.09，接近random——因为MMLU-CF 本身的contamination annotation也有噪声（它只标注了\\\"显著修改\\\"的items，但并未验证原始items 确实被contaminated），加上DIF flags被spurious signal淹没，两个noisy signal之间几乎无相关。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"对比DIF与传统检测器在包含/不包含RL-trained模型的cohort上的表现差异。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dif_tpr_sft_only_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.42,\n      \"dif_tpr_with_rl_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.29,\n      \"dif_power_retention_ratio\": 0.69,\n      \"traditional_mink_auroc_sft\": 0.74,\n      \"traditional_mink_auroc_rl\": 0.58,\n      \"traditional_constat_auroc_sft\": 0.71,\n      \"traditional_constat_auroc_rl\": 0.61,\n      \"traditional_dvd_auroc_sft\": 0.68,\n      \"traditional_dvd_auroc_rl\": 0.55,\n      \"dif_auroc_sft\": 0.67,\n      \"dif_auroc_rl\": 0.54,\n      \"dif_vs_traditional_auroc_gap_under_rl\": 0.02,\n      \"n_rl_models_available\": 12,\n      \"rl_model_cohort_size\": 12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 3: RL-Robustness Comparison — DIF vs Traditional Detectors\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"auroc_sft_cohort\",\n          \"auroc_rl_cohort\",\n          \"retention_ratio\",\n          \"delta_auroc\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DIF_ETS_C\",\n            0.67,\n            0.54,\n            0.81,\n            -0.13\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Min-K%\",\n            0.74,\n            0.58,\n            0.78,\n            -0.16\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat\",\n            0.71,\n            0.61,\n            0.86,\n            -0.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DVD\",\n            0.68,\n            0.55,\n            0.81,\n            -0.13\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Perplexity\",\n            0.69,\n            0.56,\n            0.81,\n            -0.13\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 4: DIF TPR Under SFT vs RL Cohorts\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"effect_size\",\n          \"tpr_sft_only\",\n          \"tpr_with_rl\",\n          \"retention\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"δ≥1.6\",\n            0.48,\n            0.35,\n            0.73\n          ],\n          [\n            \"δ≥1.4\",\n            0.42,\n            0.29,\n            0.69\n          ],\n          [\n            \"δ≥1.0\",\n            0.2,\n            0.13,\n            0.65\n          ],\n          [\n            \"δ≥0.6\",\n            0.09,\n            0.06,\n            0.67\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DIF的RL-robustness优势不显著。AUROC under RL: DIF 0.54 vs best traditional 0.61 (ConStat)， DIF实际上略差于ConStat。Power retention ratio 0.69落在worst tier预测范围[0.5, 0.75]内。 核心问题：RL改变ICC形状（discrimination parameter a也变化），不仅仅是difficulty shift， 这意味着DIF的理论robustness argument不成立。加上RL cohort sample size仅12，统计结论的 可靠性本身存疑。无法支撑paper的headline claim。\\n\\n\\nRL-robustness假设的理论基础是\\\"DIF操作在group-level ICC上，RL只平移不改变ICC形状\\\"。但worst 情景下RL不仅平移ICC——GRPO/PPO通过reward shaping改变了模型在不同difficulty levels上的response pattern，导致ICC形状本身变化（slope变陡或变平）。这使得RL-trained模型与SFT模型之间的ICC差异 既来自contamination也来自training method，DIF无法区分二者。DIF在RL cohort下power从0.42降到 0.29（retention ratio=0.69），传统方法从~0.71降到~0.58。关键是DIF的降幅比例与传统方法相当， AUROC差距仅0.02——不足以支撑\\\"DIF是RL-orthogonal signal\\\"的核心论点。此外，可获取的RL模型 仅12个（METABENCH中标注为RL-trained的开源模型有限），cohort太小导致DIF统计功效本身就低， 难以将power loss归因于RL vs simply small N。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"独立评估ConStat-style perturbation testing在MMLU上的contamination检测能力。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_0.6\": 0.32,\n      \"constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_1.0\": 0.45,\n      \"constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.55,\n      \"constat_tpr_rl_delta_ge_0.6\": 0.11,\n      \"constat_tpr_rl_delta_ge_1.0\": 0.18,\n      \"constat_fpr\": 0.06,\n      \"constat_fdr_controlled_power\": 0.28,\n      \"n_perturbation_items_generated\": 220,\n      \"perturbation_quality_human_equiv_rate\": 0.82,\n      \"paraphrase_semantic_similarity\": 0.91\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 5: ConStat Perturbation Detection by Effect Size and Model Type\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"effect_size\",\n          \"tpr_sft\",\n          \"tpr_rl\",\n          \"tpr_mixed\",\n          \"fpr\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"δ≥1.4\",\n            0.55,\n            0.18,\n            0.38,\n            0.06\n          ],\n          [\n            \"δ≥1.0\",\n            0.45,\n            0.14,\n            0.3,\n            0.06\n          ],\n          [\n            \"δ≥0.6\",\n            0.32,\n            0.11,\n            0.22,\n            0.07\n          ],\n          [\n            \"δ≥0.4\",\n            0.19,\n            0.08,\n            0.14,\n            0.07\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ConStat在non-RL场景下对large effects有moderate power，但RL场景下急剧退化。作为ensemble component对non-RL覆盖有限值，但无法作为RL-robust complement to DIF（两者在RL下都弱）。 FDR-controlled power 0.28意味着实际可用的detection capacity很有限。\\n\\n\\nConStat在non-RL模型上有中等检测力（TPR=0.32 for δ≥0.6），因为SFT模型对verbatim memorized items的perturbation确实敏感——答对原题但答错改写题是contamination的合理信号。 但在worst tier下：(1) 真实contamination多为partial memorization，模型可能只记住了answer pattern而非exact wording，对perturbation同样答对，降低sensitivity；(2) LLM paraphrase 生成的reformulations质量参差——82%被判为semantically equivalent，但18%引入了微妙的 difficulty变化，增加noise；(3) RL模型对perturbation的sensitivity本身就低（RL鼓励 generalization），RL场景下TPR骤降至0.11。FDR-controlled power仅0.28，意味着在控制 false discovery rate后，能检出的contaminated items不到三分之一。作为standalone result 有一定baseline价值，但不足以独立成章。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"独立评估DVD generation variance方法在MMLU上检测variant contamination的能力。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dvd_tpr_variant_contamination\": 0.22,\n      \"dvd_tpr_verbatim_contamination\": 0.48,\n      \"dvd_tpr_partial_contamination\": 0.12,\n      \"dvd_fpr\": 0.09,\n      \"dvd_auroc_overall\": 0.61,\n      \"n_models_evaluated\": 13,\n      \"n_items_sampled\": 500,\n      \"responses_per_item\": 50,\n      \"bimodal_distribution_rate_contaminated\": 0.18,\n      \"bimodal_distribution_rate_clean\": 0.07,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 65\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 6: DVD Detection by Contamination Type\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"contamination_type\",\n          \"tpr\",\n          \"fpr\",\n          \"auroc\",\n          \"n_items\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"verbatim\",\n            0.48,\n            0.09,\n            0.72,\n            120\n          ],\n          [\n            \"variant\",\n            0.22,\n            0.09,\n            0.58,\n            180\n          ],\n          [\n            \"partial\",\n            0.12,\n            0.09,\n            0.52,\n            200\n          ],\n          [\n            \"overall\",\n            0.25,\n            0.09,\n            0.61,\n            500\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DVD对variant contamination的检测力远低于预期（TPR=0.22 vs 论文claim需要的高coverage）。 核心问题是real-world contamination不产生clean bimodal response pattern——partial memorization 导致diffuse variance而非bimodal variance。GPU开销大但回报低，作为ensemble component 贡献有限。\\n\\n\\nDVD的理论基础是contaminated items上model generation variance呈bimodal分布（有时recall memorized answer，有时不能）。在worst tier下：(1) variant contamination（题目被改写后 contaminated）信号最弱——模型对variant的memorization不稳定，generation variance与clean items差异小，TPR仅0.22；(2) partial contamination（仅记住部分信息）几乎无法检测（TPR=0.12）， 因为partial memory不产生bimodal response pattern，而是持续的uncertainty；(3) 即使verbatim contamination，TPR也仅0.48，因为很多模型在temperature sampling下对已知答案也表现stable （always correct），generation variance反而很低——与clean but easy items难以区分；(4) bimodal rate在contaminated items上仅18% vs clean items 7%，差异有统计显著性但effect size 太小无法做reliable detection。FPR=0.09偏高。总计消耗65 GPU hours，性价比低。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n    \"description\": \"将DIF + ConStat + DVD融合为多信号ensemble，评估覆盖度和precision。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ensemble_tpr_full_spectrum\": 0.42,\n      \"ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.52,\n      \"ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_1.0\": 0.3,\n      \"ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_0.6\": 0.18,\n      \"ensemble_fpr\": 0.11,\n      \"ensemble_f1\": 0.35,\n      \"majority_voting_tpr\": 0.38,\n      \"weighted_fusion_tpr\": 0.42,\n      \"signal_correlation_dif_constat\": 0.61,\n      \"signal_correlation_dif_dvd\": 0.54,\n      \"signal_correlation_constat_dvd\": 0.58,\n      \"unique_items_flagged_by_only_one_signal_pct\": 0.15,\n      \"items_flagged_by_all_three_pct\": 0.42\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 7: Ensemble vs Individual Signal Performance\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"tpr_ge_1.4\",\n          \"tpr_ge_1.0\",\n          \"tpr_ge_0.6\",\n          \"fpr\",\n          \"f1\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DIF_only\",\n            0.38,\n            0.18,\n            0.09,\n            0.12,\n            0.25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat_only\",\n            0.38,\n            0.3,\n            0.22,\n            0.06,\n            0.32\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DVD_only\",\n            0.25,\n            0.15,\n            0.1,\n            0.09,\n            0.18\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Majority_2of3\",\n            0.38,\n            0.19,\n            0.11,\n            0.05,\n            0.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Weighted_fusion\",\n            0.52,\n            0.3,\n            0.18,\n            0.11,\n            0.35\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 8: Signal Correlation Matrix\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"signal_pair\",\n          \"pearson_r\",\n          \"overlap_in_flagged_items_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DIF-ConStat\",\n            0.61,\n            0.68\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DIF-DVD\",\n            0.54,\n            0.59\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat-DVD\",\n            0.58,\n            0.63\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Ensemble的\\\"互补覆盖\\\"核心假设不成立。信号间高相关（0.54-0.61）意味着ensemble主要在置信度上 提升（对已检出items更confident）而非在覆盖度上提升（检出新items）。Weighted fusion的TPR=0.42 仅比best individual signal (ConStat 0.30 at δ≥1.0) 提升有限，且FPR=0.11偏高。这个ensemble 不能作为\\\"full-spectrum detection system\\\"呈现——更准确的描述是\\\"three weak signals with correlated failure modes\\\"。\\n\\n\\nEnsemble假设三个signal互补——DIF覆盖large effects+RL场景，ConStat覆盖non-RL medium effects， DVD覆盖variant contamination。但worst tier下：(1) 三个signal之间correlation高（r=0.54-0.61）， 表明它们largely flag同一批items而非互补覆盖不同盲区；(2) 仅15%的items被unique地由某一个 signal单独检出，说明\\\"互补覆盖\\\"理论不成立——各signal的failure modes相关（都在partial/medium effect上失败）；(3) 42%的items被三个signal同时flag，说明easy cases三者都能检出但hard cases 三者都漏检；(4) FPR=0.11，majority voting无法有效压低FPR因为false positives也呈相关模式 （architecture-driven spurious DIF也往往在perturbation testing中产生false positive）。 Weighted fusion比majority voting略好（TPR 0.42 vs 0.38）但提升有限。整体full-spectrum TPR=0.42落在worst tier [0.35, 0.6]范围内，不足以作为实用detection system。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n    \"description\": \"在GSM8K上复制DIF分析，以GSM1K作为contamination ground truth进行交叉验证。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gsm8k_gsm1k_gap_dif_correlation_spearman\": 0.11,\n      \"gsm8k_gsm1k_gap_dif_correlation_pearson\": 0.08,\n      \"dif_tpr_gsm8k_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.3,\n      \"dif_fpr_gsm8k\": 0.13,\n      \"n_models_with_both_gsm8k_gsm1k\": 48,\n      \"irt_model_fit_rmsea_gsm8k\": 0.09,\n      \"gsm8k_item_discrimination_mean\": 0.85,\n      \"gsm1k_gap_mean_across_models\": 0.07,\n      \"gsm1k_gap_std\": 0.11,\n      \"n_items_gsm8k_analyzed\": 1319\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 9: GSM8K Cross-Validation Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"value\",\n          \"worst_tier_range\",\n          \"verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DIF_TPR_δ≥1.4\",\n            0.3,\n            \"0.25-0.50\",\n            \"IN_RANGE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DIF_FPR\",\n            0.13,\n            \"0.08-0.15\",\n            \"IN_RANGE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K-GSM1K_gap_correlation\",\n            0.11,\n            \"0.0-0.18\",\n            \"IN_RANGE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"N_models\",\n            48,\n            \"≥50 desired\",\n            \"INSUFFICIENT\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"IRT_fit_RMSEA\",\n            0.09,\n            \"≤0.06\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark validation为negative result。GSM8K上DIF表现与MMLU类似（low TPR, high FPR）， 且与GSM1K ground truth的correlation接近零（rho=0.11）。样本量不足（48 models vs desired 50+） 进一步削弱统计结论的可靠性。这不能作为DIF generalizability的支撑证据。\\n\\n\\nGSM8K validation在worst tier下面临多重困难：(1) 可获取的同时有GSM8K和GSM1K结果的模型仅 约48个（远少于MMLU的5055个），DIF统计功效严重不足；(2) GSM8K是math benchmark，item discrimination偏低(mean a=0.85)因为数学题的对错更binary、less informative about latent ability gradient，这直接降低DIF detection power；(3) GSM8K-GSM1K gap本身noisy（std=0.11 vs mean=0.07），gap的model-level variance高说明contamination不是uniform的——不同模型 contamination程度差异大，但DIF是item-level metric，model-level gap与item-level DIF flag之间的mapping本就不是直接对应的；(4) GSM1K作为ground truth的assumption是\\\"GSM1K uncontaminated\\\"，但GSM1K发布后也可能被contaminated，ground truth本身会退化。 Spearman rho=0.11几乎无相关，无法支撑cross-benchmark generalizability。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n    \"description\": \"在METABENCH MMLU数据上拟合bifactor IRT模型，选取anchor items，执行equating pilot。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bifactor_convergence\": \"partial\",\n      \"bifactor_iterations_to_convergence\": 8500,\n      \"bifactor_n_items_converged\": 9200,\n      \"bifactor_n_items_failed\": 3308,\n      \"general_factor_variance_explained\": 0.35,\n      \"n_specific_factors\": 57,\n      \"specific_factor_avg_loading\": 0.28,\n      \"anchor_item_n_selected\": 380,\n      \"anchor_item_stability_mean_dif\": 0.15,\n      \"equating_spearman_rho_before\": 0.82,\n      \"equating_spearman_rho_after\": 0.85,\n      \"equating_rank_displacement_mean\": 3.2,\n      \"equating_rank_displacement_p95\": 12,\n      \"score_reliability_original\": 0.94,\n      \"score_reliability_equated\": 0.89\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 10: Bifactor IRT Model Fit and Equating Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"value\",\n          \"target\",\n          \"verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"convergence_rate\",\n            \"73.5%\",\n            \"≥95%\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"general_factor_variance\",\n            0.35,\n            \"≥0.50\",\n            \"WEAK\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"anchor_items_available\",\n            380,\n            \"≥500\",\n            \"MARGINAL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"equating_rho\",\n            0.85,\n            \"≥0.95\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"rank_displacement_p95\",\n            12,\n            \"≤5\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"score_reliability_post\",\n            0.89,\n            \"≥0.92\",\n            \"MARGINAL\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 11: Factor Structure Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"factor_type\",\n          \"n_factors\",\n          \"mean_loading\",\n          \"pct_items_loading_gt_0.3\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"general\",\n            1,\n            0.42,\n            \"62%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"specific_STEM\",\n            14,\n            0.31,\n            \"38%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"specific_humanities\",\n            18,\n            0.26,\n            \"29%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"specific_social_science\",\n            15,\n            0.28,\n            \"33%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"specific_other\",\n            10,\n            0.24,\n            \"25%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bifactor model在异构LLM population上partially converges但factor structure不清晰。 General factor太弱（35% variance）挑战了\\\"MMLU measures a coherent construct\\\"的前提。 Equating产生了modest improvement (0.82→0.85) 但远未达到psychometric equivalence标准 (0.95)。作为独立贡献（Claim 3 standalone），这个result需要被framed为\\\"benchmark multidimensionality的empirical characterization\\\"而非\\\"successful equating\\\"。可能可以 pivot到Growing Pains style的\\\"LLM evaluation需要multidimensional IRT\\\"叙事。\\n\\n\\nBifactor model在5055个异构模型上面临严重的estimation challenge：(1) 57个MMLU subjects作为 specific factors，加上1个general factor，parameter space巨大（~12500 items × 3 parameters × 58 factors），在worst tier下3308个items（26%）的参数估计不收敛或产生Heywood cases （negative variance estimates）；(2) general factor仅解释35%的variance——这意味着MMLU 不是primarily measuring一个general LLM ability，而是highly multidimensional的，bifactor structure不是good fit；(3) specific factor loadings平均仅0.28，说明subject-level factors 也很弱，很多items不清晰地load在任何factor上——factor structure不可解释；(4) 尽管如此， equating在技术上仍可执行：选出380个stable anchor items（无DIF、参数估计收敛），equating 后ranking correlation从0.82提升到0.85，但这个提升幅度小（Δ=0.03），且基线rho=0.82 已低于Claim 3要求的0.95标准。Equating没有失败但也没有convincingly成功——它能small improvement ranking stability，但不能达到psychometric equivalence的标准。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n    \"description\": \"生成替代items并通过student simulation进行calibration，评估difficulty estimation质量。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_items_generated\": 150,\n      \"n_items_passing_quality_filter\": 112,\n      \"difficulty_calibration_rho_student_sim\": 0.48,\n      \"difficulty_calibration_rho_prompt_based\": 0.22,\n      \"difficulty_mae_student_sim\": 0.85,\n      \"difficulty_mae_prompt_based\": 1.45,\n      \"discrimination_calibration_rho\": 0.31,\n      \"construct_alignment_rate\": 0.72,\n      \"holdout_validation_rho\": 0.44,\n      \"student_sim_correlation_with_real_models\": 0.52,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 180\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 12: Item Calibration Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"difficulty_rho\",\n          \"difficulty_mae\",\n          \"discrimination_rho\",\n          \"construct_alignment\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"student_simulation\",\n            0.48,\n            0.85,\n            0.31,\n            \"72%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"prompt_based\",\n            0.22,\n            1.45,\n            0.18,\n            \"65%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random_baseline\",\n            0.05,\n            1.8,\n            0.08,\n            \"45%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 13: Holdout Validation on 30 Models\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"student_sim\",\n          \"prompt_based\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"difficulty_rank_correlation\",\n            0.44,\n            0.19\n          ],\n          [\n            \"score_equivalence_rho\",\n            0.78,\n            0.68\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ranking_preservation_top10\",\n            \"70%\",\n            \"50%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Student simulation在MMLU上的calibration quality不足以支撑reliable item replacement。 Difficulty rho=0.48意味着替换后的benchmark与原版在difficulty ordering上只有moderate agreement，不够做psychometric equating。但student sim vs prompt-based的comparison （0.48 vs 0.22）以及failure mode analysis（which subjects/difficulty ranges失败） 仍有独立的文献贡献价值。\\n\\n\\nItem generation在worst tier下的核心问题：(1) Student simulation (arXiv 2601.09953) 的difficulty estimation在MMLU上表现弱于其在其他benchmarks上的reported results——因为 MMLU covers 57 diverse subjects，student simulation的\\\"simulated students\\\"是single LLM 做capability ablation，但不同subject需要不同type的knowledge/reasoning，single-model simulation无法capture this diversity，rho=0.48；(2) Prompt-based difficulty targeting 依然很差（rho=0.22），与文献报告一致；(3) Student simulation比prompt-based好（0.48 vs 0.22） 但absolute accuracy仍不够——difficulty MAE=0.85 logits意味着平均偏差接近1个标准差， 生成的items实际difficulty与target可能差1-2个difficulty band；(4) Discrimination calibration 更差（rho=0.31），因为discrimination是更subtle的item property，依赖于item如何在不同ability levels上区分模型，student simulation几乎无法capture；(5) Construct alignment rate 72% 意味着28%的generated items虽然表面上是同一subject但实际测量的cognitive process不同 （e.g., 要求recall的item被替换为要求reasoning的item）。这些result不支撑\\\"calibrated item regeneration\\\"的claim，但student sim vs prompt-based的comparison本身有文献价值。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"实现cumulative Bayesian DIF priors，模拟4次successive benchmark administrations的power积累。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"single_admin_power_delta_1.0\": 0.15,\n      \"cumulative_power_2_admins_delta_1.0\": 0.22,\n      \"cumulative_power_3_admins_delta_1.0\": 0.3,\n      \"cumulative_power_4_admins_delta_1.0\": 0.38,\n      \"single_admin_power_delta_1.4\": 0.35,\n      \"cumulative_power_4_admins_delta_1.4\": 0.55,\n      \"bayesian_fpr_single\": 0.1,\n      \"bayesian_fpr_cumulative_4\": 0.08,\n      \"prior_informativeness_shrinkage\": 0.45\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 14: Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power Accumulation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n_administrations\",\n          \"power_delta_1.0\",\n          \"power_delta_1.4\",\n          \"fpr\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            0.15,\n            0.35,\n            0.1\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            0.22,\n            0.42,\n            0.09\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            0.3,\n            0.49,\n            0.09\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.38,\n            0.55,\n            0.08\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cumulative Bayesian approach有边际收益但无法rescue低baseline power。4 admins后power 仅从0.15升至0.38 (δ=1.0)，远低于theoretical 0.70。Population heterogeneity导致prior transfer效率低。作为P2 experiment，结果不改变overall narrative但进一步确认了DIF在 heterogeneous LLM population上的fundamental limitations。\\n\\n\\nBayesian cumulative priors在worst tier下受到两个因素制约：(1) 如果baseline single-admin power已经很低（0.15 for δ=1.0，因为real data上IRT model misfit），那么cumulative evidence accumulation的起点就低——Bayesian updating from a weak prior仍然是weak， 4次admin后仅到0.38（远低于theoretical prediction of 0.70）；(2) Prior informativeness 受model population heterogeneity影响——如果每次administration的model cohort composition 很不同（architecture mix变化），prior从上一admin的posterior transfer不顺畅，shrinkage factor高达0.45（理想应<0.2），意味着prior对posterior的influence被data overwhelm但data 本身noisy。FPR从0.10降至0.08是modest improvement。总体而言，cumulative approach能 提升power但幅度远不如simulated homogeneous scenarios中的预期。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"分析benchmark在progressive item replacement下的validity degradation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ranking_stability_5pct_replaced\": 0.94,\n      \"ranking_stability_10pct_replaced\": 0.88,\n      \"ranking_stability_20pct_replaced\": 0.79,\n      \"ranking_stability_50pct_replaced\": 0.62,\n      \"score_reliability_5pct\": 0.92,\n      \"score_reliability_10pct\": 0.88,\n      \"score_reliability_20pct\": 0.81,\n      \"score_reliability_50pct\": 0.67,\n      \"construct_coverage_5pct\": 0.97,\n      \"construct_coverage_10pct\": 0.93,\n      \"construct_coverage_20pct\": 0.85,\n      \"construct_coverage_50pct\": 0.71,\n      \"critical_replacement_threshold\": 0.12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 15: Validity Degradation Under Progressive Replacement\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"replacement_pct\",\n          \"ranking_rho\",\n          \"reliability\",\n          \"construct_coverage\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0% (baseline)\",\n            1.0,\n            0.94,\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5%\",\n            0.94,\n            0.92,\n            0.97\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10%\",\n            0.88,\n            0.88,\n            0.93\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            0.79,\n            0.81,\n            0.85\n          ],\n          [\n            \"50%\",\n            0.62,\n            0.67,\n            0.71\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 16: Critical Thresholds\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"validity_criterion\",\n          \"threshold_value\",\n          \"max_safe_replacement_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"ranking_rho_≥0.90\",\n            0.9,\n            \"12%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"reliability_≥0.90\",\n            0.9,\n            \"7%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"construct_coverage_≥0.90\",\n            0.9,\n            \"14%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"all_criteria_met\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"7%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Graceful degradation analysis表明在当前calibration quality下，只能安全替换7%的items （约875个items，满足所有validity criteria）。这远不足以构成practical \\\"self-healing\\\" benchmark——如果检测到的contaminated items超过7%，replacement会损害benchmark validity。 这是对Claim 3的严重限制，但degradation curve本身是有价值的empirical contribution， 可以frame为\\\"item replacement的practical bounds\\\"。\\n\\n\\nGraceful degradation在worst tier下退化快于预期因为：(1) Item calibration quality差 （difficulty rho=0.48 from plan_006），替换items的psychometric properties与被替换items 不匹配，每次替换引入的error大于calibration error budget允许的范围；(2) Bifactor equating 不充分（rho=0.85 from plan_005），equating本身引入systematic bias，累积到20%替换时 ranking stability降至0.79（如果equating完美，应维持在0.92+）；(3) Construct coverage degradation因为28%的generated items construct alignment有问题（from plan_006）， 20%替换时约5-6%的items测量不同construct，coverage降至0.85。Critical threshold（ranking rho降至0.90以下的替换比例）仅12%——意味着实际上只能安全替换约1500个items，远少于 potential contaminated items的数量（如果FPR=0.12则约1800个被flag）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n    \"description\": \"实现Item-Focused Trees，将model release date作为continuous covariate替代categorical cohort DIF。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ift_tpr_delta_ge_1.4\": 0.33,\n      \"ift_tpr_delta_ge_1.0\": 0.16,\n      \"ift_fpr\": 0.1,\n      \"ift_vs_categorical_dif_tpr_delta\": -0.05,\n      \"ift_computation_time_hours\": 18,\n      \"n_splits_found\": 3.2,\n      \"split_dates_concentration\": \"2023-06 to 2024-01\",\n      \"overfitting_cross_val_tpr_drop\": 0.12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 17: Item-Focused Trees vs Categorical DIF\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"categorical_dif\",\n          \"ift\",\n          \"delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"TPR_δ≥1.4\",\n            0.38,\n            0.33,\n            -0.05\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TPR_δ≥1.0\",\n            0.18,\n            0.16,\n            -0.02\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FPR\",\n            0.12,\n            0.1,\n            -0.02\n          ],\n          [\n            \"F1\",\n            0.25,\n            0.24,\n            -0.01\n          ],\n          [\n            \"computation_hours\",\n            0.5,\n            18,\n            \"+17.5\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"IFT未能改善DIF detection。Split points与architecture transitions而非contamination events 对齐，进一步证实model heterogeneity是dominant signal source。计算成本高36倍但无performance gain。作为P2 experiment，结论是negative：continuous covariate treatment不解决fundamental 问题。\\n\\nItem-Focused Trees理论上避免arbitrary cohort splits，但在worst tier下：(1) Release date 作为continuous covariate与contamination的关系不是smooth monotonic的——contamination是 event-driven（某次data leak），不是gradual trend，IFT的tree structure可以capture这个 但容易overfit到特定split points；(2) Cross-validation显示TPR drop=0.12，说明overfitting significant；(3) 在model heterogeneity高的情况下，IFT实际上比categorical DIF表现略差 （TPR差-0.05），因为tree splitting在high-noise环境下容易找到spurious splits——3.2个 average splits集中在2023年中到2024年初，这恰好是architecture transition period （GPT-4发布后大量models涌现），tree可能在capture architecture shift而非contamination。 FPR=0.10比categorical DIF（0.12）略低，但improvement不显著。Computation cost 18 hours 因为per-item tree fitting在12508 items上。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":901,"startLine":1,"totalLines":901}}}
